{
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Sid": "DenyDisableCloudTrail",
            "Effect": "Deny",
            "Action": [
                "cloudtrail:StopLogging",
                "cloudtrail:DeleteTrail",
                "cloudtrail:UpdateTrail"
            ],
            "Resource": "*"
        }
    ]
}


##What does this JSON policy do?
Prevents anyone — even account administrators with full privileges — from disabling, modifying, or deleting audit logs. This is critical for compliance in highly regulated environments (like a fintech company), ensuring that a malicious actor cannot turn off the cloudtrail before attempting a breach, keeping the forensic record immutable.


